.\" Leon Build Tool — Man Page
.TH LBT 1 "2026-08-02" "lbt 0.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lbt \- Leon Build Tool: author and preview boot themes, run plugins, manage boot config
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lbt
.B info
.RI [ dump ]
.br
.B lbt
.B discover
.RI [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B lbt
.B theme
.B list | preview
.I name
.RI [ dump ]
.B | run
.I name
.RI [ dump ]
.br
.B lbt
.B plugin
.B list | run
.I name
.I func
.RI [ args ... ]
.br
.B lbt
.B tui
.RI [ run
.RI [ name ]
.B | apply
.I name
.B | list ]
.br
.B lbt
.B config
.B get
.RI [ key ]
.B | set
.I key
.I value
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lbt
is the host-side companion to the Leon bootloader. It introspects the live
machine (block devices, EFI System Partitions, boot entries, framebuffer and
BGRT logo geometry), renders boot themes against real or dumped geometry, runs
Leon plugins, launches full-screen TUIs (a keyboard-driven boot-manager menu
ships as the default), and edits the boot configuration consumed by the
bootloader.
.br
Theme and plugin registration is delegated to the shared cps engine
(see
.BR cps (1)),
so whatever is registered there (t.desc / p.desc) is available to
.BR lbt .
The theme, plugin, and tui commands require the
.I python
build feature (what
.B "make build"
produces); a plain
.B "cargo build -p lbt"
links no Python code and omits them.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS info
Print the current framebuffer and BGRT logo geometry.
.TP
.B info \fIdump\
With a path to a geometry record (\fIbootinfo.json\fR written by the
bootloader to \eEFI\eleon), print the captured geometry instead of the live one.
.TP
.B info
Without an argument, read live geometry from /sys
(/sys/class/graphics/fb0 and /sys/firmware/acpi/bgrt). Fails loudly if no live
framebuffer is available rather than guessing.
.SS discover
Auto-detect every EFI System Partition and its boot entries.
Note: In addition to enumerating mounted ESPs, Leon scans common `/boot`
locations (`/boot`, `/boot/efi`, `/boot/EFI`) for EFI-capable files and
includes them as candidate boot entries. Detection is strict: `.efi` files
must validate as PE/COFF (`MZ` + `PE\0\0`) and ELF files must contain the
`EFI stub` marker in the first 64 KiB to be accepted as an EFI-stub kernel.
.TP
.B discover
List block devices (name, kind, filesystem, mount point), ESPs, and boot entries.
.TP
.B discover \-\-json
Emit the same information as machine-readable JSON with the keys
.BR devices ,
.BR esps ,
and
.BR boot_entries .
.SS theme
.TP
.B theme list
List registered boot themes.
.TP
.B theme preview \fIname\fR \fI[dump]\fR
Render a theme's splash and menu against Leon geometry (live sysfs, or a
geometry record), without touching the display.
.TP
.B theme run \fIname\fR \fI[dump]\fR
Invoke a theme's full-screen
.IR run ()
program.
.SS plugin
.TP
.B plugin list
List registered plugins.
.TP
.B plugin run \fIname\fR \fIfunc\fR \fI[args ...]\fR
Run a plugin function (by name or alias) with the given arguments.
.SS tui
.TP
.B tui
.RI [ run
.RI [ name ]
.B | apply
.I name
.B | list ]
.TP
.B tui
or
.B "tui run"
Run the configured default TUI (the
.I [python] tui
path in
.I ~/.config/leon/python.toml
). When none is configured, the shipped Leon boot-manager menu runs — it is
embedded in the binary and materialized to
.I ~/.config/leon/tuis/leon_menu.py
on first use.
.TP
.B "tui run" \fIname\fR
Run the registered TUI \fIname\fR (from
.I t.desc
) instead.
.TP
.B "tui list"
List registered TUIs.
.TP
.B "tui apply" \fIname\fR
Persist a TUI as the default in
.I ~/.config/leon/python.toml
(absolute path, \fItui_mode\fR pinned to \fBfalse\fR) and print the stored
path.
.PP
Before a TUI runs, lbt exports the live framebuffer + BGRT geometry, the
discovered boot entries, and the boot config as
.I LEON_*
environment variables (see the header of
.I ~/.config/leon/tuis/leon_menu.py
). The menu is pure stdlib (no curses) and uses the full keymap: arrows and
.I hjkl
to move, PgUp/PgDn, Home/End, \fI1-9\fR/\fI0\fR to jump,
.I /
to search with
.I n
/
.I N
for next/previous match, Tab/Shift+Tab to move focus, Enter or space for a
boot preview, and
.I q
/ Esc / Ctrl+C to quit. Geometry or entries may be absent (no framebuffer, no
mounted ESP) — the menu shows a friendly placeholder state.
.SS config
.TP
.B config get \fI[key]\fR
Print one boot config key, or all keys when omitted.
.TP
.B config set \fIkey\fR \fIvalue\fR
Set a boot config key. Supported keys:
.IR timeout ,
.IR default_entry ,
.IR theme ,
.IR splash ,
.IR entries_file
(the former must be
.B true
or
.BR false ).
The new value is written to
.I ~/.config/leon/boot.toml
and mirrored onto every mounted EFI System Partition as
.IR \eEFI\eleon\eboot.toml ,
which is what the bootloader reads at boot.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/leon/boot.toml
Host copy of the boot configuration (timeout, default_entry, theme, splash,
entries_file) written by
.BR "lbt config set" .
If absent,
.B config get
falls back to the copy on a mounted ESP.
.TP
.I \eEFI\eleon\eboot.toml
The copy the bootloader actually reads, kept on the boot volume (ESP) and
validated by it at every boot; a missing or broken file simply yields
defaults.
.TP
.I \eEFI\eleon\ebootinfo.json
Geometry + resolved config record written by the bootloader at boot time;
consumed by
.B lbt info
and
.BR lbt " theme preview/run" .
.TP
.I \eEFI\eleon\eentries.jsonc
Boot entries discovered and written by the bootloader at every boot; consumed
by
.BR lbt " discover" .
.TP
.I ~/.config/leon/python.toml
Host Python config for the cps engine (\fIenabled\fR, \fItui\fR, \fItheme\fR,
\fIvenv_path\fR, \fItui_mode\fR). Relative \fItui\fR/\fIvenv_path\fR paths
resolve against this file's directory, never the working directory.
.TP
.I ~/.config/leon/tuis/leon_menu.py
The shipped boot-manager TUI, materialized from the embedded copy on first
use; edit it to customize the default menu.
.TP
.I t.desc , p.desc
Descriptor files registering themes, TUIs and plugins for the shared cps
engine. The first parseable file in
.IR ~/.config/leon ,
.IR /etc/leon ,
and the current directory wins; the repo ships a default
.I t.desc
registering the Leon menu.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lbl (1),
.BR leon-common (7),
.BR cps (1)
